-- title:
--   Per-node conclusion frame for descended semistable nodes
-- statement:
--   This module defines a single Prop-valued predicate, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.PernodeConclusion`](../def/ModularCurve_PernodeConclusion.html#L29), which packages the local assertion made at one node of the descended model. Its arguments are a prime $q$, a level $M'\ne 0$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ over the residue field $\kappa_A$ of $A$, a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ from the base-changed level-$M'$ function field to that field, a chosen $s\in W$, a subfield $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with an element $\pi_0$ lying in $A$, a prime $\ell'$, a subfield $K_\ell$ of the Laurent series field over $k_0$ with a nonzero element $j_\ell$, the hypothesis that the level-$q\ell'$ $j$-expansion `jqNModC k₀ (q * ℓ')` lies in $K_\ell$, a constant $a_0\in A_0:=A\cap k_0$, a subfield $K_0\subseteq K_\ell$ over $k_0$, a subalgebra $B_0\subseteq K_\ell$, a valuation subring $W_0'$ of $K_0$, a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $K_0$ and one subring $\mathcal O$, together with further ambient data of the descent situation ($\ell,\zeta_0,\varpi_t,K_b,A_b,\varpi_b,\xi$, an ideal $y$, a subalgebra $B_t$, a valuation subring $W_t$, integers $n,m$, $\gamma_0\in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the completion of $A_0$, a finite set `ends` and a subgroup $G$), summarised here; the body constrains the first group.
--
--   The predicate asserts: $\mathcal O\subseteq W_0'$; $\mathcal O$ is local and Noetherian, meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, and every element of $\mathcal O$ is congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $A_0$ (so its residue field is that of $A_0$). Next, there is $E_0\ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{2w}v$ for a unit $v$ of $A_0$, where $w=\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, together with $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$, a unit $u$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion $\hat{\mathcal O}$ with the crossing model $\hat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ carrying constants to constants, such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ and $\iota(c_x),\iota(c_y)$ are unit multiples of $U$ and $V$; $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$ and $c_x$, when it lies in $W_0'$, is a unit there. Further, $j_{q\ell'}-a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $\mathcal O$, with $\iota$ of it a unit times $V^e$ for some $e\ge 1$. There is a valuation subring $W_x\supseteq\mathcal O$ of $K_0$ meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, containing an element whose reduction satisfies no relation with $A$-integral coefficients, with $c_x$ a non-unit and $c_y$ a unit; on $W_x$ the level-$M'$ dictionary holds: any $g$ in the full level-$M'$ function field which is $R_0$-integral and has no pole where $j_q$ has none has its $\ell'$-expansion in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lying in the maximal ideal exactly when $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g)$ vanishes, and, when that residue is finite at $s$, lying in $\mathcal O$ with residue the value $s(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(g))$; moreover every other $\mathcal O'\in$ `nodes` contains an element outside $W_x$. Finally there is a subring $B_x\subseteq\mathcal O$ mapping into $B_0$, regular wherever $j_\ell$ is, with $\mathcal O$ its localisation at the elements of $B_x$ that are units in $\mathcal O$, with fraction field $K_0$, generated over the constants by a finite set, and containing an element $b$ having a pole at every valuation subring of $K_0$ which has constants $A_0$, residually kills $\pi_0$, receives $j$ residually transcendentally, and fails to contain $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** The predicate is assembled from Mathlib's `ValuationSubring`, `AdicCompletion`, `IsDiscreteValuationRing`, `Ideal.span` and `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal`; the crossing model $\hat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi)$ (`UVCrossingModel`, a quotient of Mathlib's `MvPowerSeries` in two variables), the reductions with prescribed constant field (`ConstantReduction`), the modular function fields and the width function `placeWidthChar` are the project's own, Mathlib having no notion of a node of a semistable model of a modular curve.
--
--   **Where it is used.** The predicate is the block asserted at each node by the descent theorem that produces, over the constants $A_0$, a semistable local picture of the full-level modular curve at $q$: each node has local ring with completed crossing model $\hat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$, one branch being the Igusa branch on which the level-$M'$ functions specialise to their values at the supersingular place $s$, the other recorded by $W_0'$, with $j_{q\ell'}-a_0$ vanishing only along the latter. Packaging it as a definition lets the statements about the descended nodes quote the whole local picture in one token.
